<title>USA: Utah Bonanza 400 MW coal unit seen restarting.</title>
<headline>Utah Bonanza 400 MW coal unit seen restarting.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1997-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The 400 megawatt (MW) Bonanza coal-fired power plant at Vernal, Utah, was in the process of resarting Monday after being shut in mid-May for scheduled maintenance, sources at the plant said.</p>
<p>The unit was expected to go off-line around mid-day for balancing, and to ramp back up around 1500 MT, they said.</p>
<p>The Bonanza plant is operated by the Deseret Generation and Transmission Cooperative.</p>
<p>((--Los Angeles bureau + 1 213 955 6761))</p>
